# .env.fleet.override — PER-SERVER overrides + additions for a fleet runner host.
#
# Copy to `.env.fleet.override` on each server and put ONLY this machine's
# specifics here:  cp .env.fleet.override.example .env.fleet.override
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   The shared base config lives in `.env.fleet` (copied from the tracked
#   `.env.fleet.preset`). When that base changes upstream, every server used to
#   have to re-copy the preset AND re-apply its local edits by hand — easy to
#   forget (a stale value here is exactly what stranded a host off the shared
#   MinIO once). Now the per-server values live HERE instead. `start-runner
#   --fleet` loads `.env.fleet` first, then this file ON TOP — and compose's
#   multiple --env-file merge is "later wins", so anything set here overrides
#   the base. This file is gitignored and is NOT touched when you re-copy the
#   preset, so updating the shared base is just:
#       git pull && cp .env.fleet.preset .env.fleet     # override survives
#
#   Anything you DON'T set here simply falls through to the shared base.

# --- REQUIRED per-server: this host's large LOCAL scratch disk --------------
# A big local POSIX path THIS server can write (staging / in-flight downloads).
# Do NOT use /Volumes/afl_data (the infra host's disk).
#   macOS: e.g. $HOME/afl_data (mkdir -p first)   Linux: e.g. /var/lib/afl_data
FW_DATA_DIR=

# --- Optional per-server: how many osm runners to start on this host --------
# Size to this machine's cores/RAM (each runner = one concurrent leaf extract).
# FW_OSM_REPLICAS=4

# --- Optional: override the infra host IP for JUST this server ---------------
# Only if this server reaches the shared MinIO/MongoDB at a different address
# than the fleet default (e.g. a NATed/remote site). Normally leave unset and
# inherit the base's FW_INFRA_IP.
# FW_INFRA_IP=<infra-host-ip>   # e.g. the infra host's LAN IP

# --- Optional: pin this server's display name / role ------------------------
# FW_RUNNER_NAME=
# FW_SERVER_GROUP=runner
